  "question": {
    "text": "If one of the diameters of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is a chord of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that, one of the diameter of the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;is a chord of another circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>Let, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the centres of the circles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The position of the two circles as shown in figure.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0062_e081d08218e0.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>It is clear from the above diagram,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a right angled triangle.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
